      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1550",
      "html": "<ul><li>Scientific name: Cteniloricaria maculata (Boeseman, 1971)</li><li>Common name: Whiptail Catfish</li><li>Type locality: Sipaliwini, upper Corantijn River basin, Suriname.</li><li>Synonyms: Harttia maculata, Parasturisoma maculata</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1550",
      "html": "<p>South America: Maroni and Corantijn River basins, including Guyana waters and the coastal rivers of Suriname and the Guianas.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1550",
      "html": "<p>Lives in creeks and rapids where the vegetation is poor, the water is clear, well-oxygenated and shallow (less than 1 m), with a sandy to rocky substrate.</p><p>Found together with Characidium fasciadorsale, Imparfinis minutus, Corydoras guianensis and especially Harttia surinamensis.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1550",
      "html": "<p>Unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
